== Effects ==
* Opens all doors in the current room, just like {{i|Dad's Key}}.

== Notes ==
* Being a [[special card]], the '''Get out of Jail Free Card''' has a significantly lower chance of appearing compared to other cards.
* Get out of Jail Free Card can open:
** {{dlc|r}} The door of a {{r|Challenge Room}} after the fight has started.
** The door to the {{E|Mega Satan}} boss fight. The door will remain open after leaving the room.
** The fight in {{r|Boss Rush}} to leave early, but cannot be used to get into the Boss Rush room if the time limit has already passed.
* Get out of Jail Free Card cannot open:
** {{dlc|nr}} The door of a {{r|Challenge Room}} after the fight has started.
** The door to {{s|???}}.
** {{a|A Strange Door}}.
** {{dlc+|r}} The flesh door to the {{E|Mom's Heart}} boss fight in {{s|Mausoleum}} II / {{s|Gehenna}} II.{{dlc-}}

== Trivia ==
* "Get out of Jail Free" is a card found in the board game ''Monopoly'', allowing its user to escape jail early. The phrase has since spread and a "Get out of Jail Free Card" is also an idiomatic expression for something that would alleviate an undesirable situation.

